Well, I suppose reverse engineering is the solution.
Which reminds me that Audiotrak have seperat drivers for Prodigy 7.1 and
Prodigy 7.1 LT, which indicates that they aren't that much alike.
According to Audiotrak there is no AC97 chip onboard, which means two
chips lesser, and 12 additional free GPIO pins on the ICE1724 chip.

Said in a other way; AudioTrak probably haven't used the same GPIO pins on
the LT model as on the ordinary Prodigy.

It looks like there is an AC97 chip on photos though.

Unfortunately there is no safe way to figure out the behavior of the GPIO
pins in software. The best thing would be to look at the board and
optionally use a voltmeter to figure out where which GPIO pin goes.

Speaking of which, the External Amplifier is located on the last stereo
output (channel 7 and 8) instead of front as on the Aureon and Prodigy 7.1
card.

